---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

// DRAFT — owner approves before publish (A8 owner prerequisites).
// The copyright section is written to match the product's actual position
// (CLAUDE.md §3.2): chord progressions and strumming patterns aren't
// copyrightable, the player authors the recipe, and we ship no song content.
const updated = 'July 2026';
const contact = 'support@rosetta.fun';
---

<Base title="Terms · Rosetta" description="The terms for using Rosetta.">
  <h1>Terms of use</h1>
  <p class="faint">Last updated: {updated}</p>

  <p>These terms cover the Rosetta app and this website. Using either means you agree to them.</p>

  <h2>Your account</h2>
  <p>
    You need an account to use Mo. Keep your sign-in details to yourself — you're responsible for what happens
    under your account. One person, one account. You must be 13 or older.
  </p>

  <h2>What you can make</h2>
  <p>
    Rosetta lets you build songs from chord progressions and strumming patterns. Those are musical building
    blocks, not recordings, and Rosetta ships no copyrighted music. What you create is yours to play, keep and
    share.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Respect other people's music.</strong> If you're recreating a song you love, that's for your own
    practice and enjoyment. Don't pass off someone else's composition as your own, and don't upload lyrics or
    recordings you don't have the rights to.
  </p>

  <h2>Mo, and what it produces</h2>
  <p>
    Mo is an AI. It gets things wrong, and two people asking for the same thing may get different results. We
    don't promise a particular song, quality level or turnaround, and we don't claim any ownership of what Mo
    makes for you.
  </p>

  <h2>Fair use of the service</h2>
  <p>
    There are limits on how many songs you can make — a monthly allowance and a daily cap that exists to stop
    abuse. Don't try to get around them, don't use automated tools against our servers, and don't use Rosetta
    to generate anything unlawful or hateful. We can suspend or delete accounts that do.
  </p>

  <h2>Paying</h2>
  <p>
    Some things cost money. Prices are shown before you buy. Purchases on this website are handled by Stripe;
    purchases in the app are handled by Apple. Subscriptions renew until you cancel — cancel any time from
    your account page (web) or from your Apple subscription settings (app). See <a href="/legal/refunds">refunds</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Credits and allowances have no cash value, can't be transferred, and are lost if you delete your account.
  </p>

  <h2>Ending things</h2>
  <p>
    You can stop using Rosetta and delete your account whenever you like. We may suspend or end an account
    that breaks these terms, or discontinue the service — if we shut it down, we'll give reasonable notice and
    refund any unused paid time.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty, and limits on liability</h2>
  <p>
    Rosetta is provided "as is". We don't guarantee it will be uninterrupted or error-free. To the extent the
    law allows, our total liability to you is limited to what you paid us in the twelve months before the
    claim. Nothing here limits liability that can't legally be limited.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update these terms. If a change is significant, we'll tell you before it takes effect.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p><a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a></p>
</Base>
